    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d344">

                <pb facs="0430" n="420" xml:id="pg420"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/7694: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-06-03T15:00:00+07:00">June 3, 1943—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 4—10:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>842. TF–127. To Secretary of Treasury from Adler. Re your 658, May 24.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Have submitted your proposals to Board and Dr. Kung and will report their
                        views on each at earliest opportunity.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Re your 1 (<hi rendition="#italic">d</hi>), I support extension of
                        permission to make remittances to Hong Kong and Shanghai Bank on following
                        grounds: (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) when and where possible it is
                        desirable to help to mitigate or counteract existing unhealthy trend towards
                        monopolization of business in hands of government or semi-government
                        institutions. This is desirable from point of view of Chinese as well as
                        foreign business interests; (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) granting
                        permission to Hong Kong and Shanghai Bank will serve as precedent for
                        subsequent inclusion of American banks which may decide to open branches in
                        free China. [Adler.]</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
